Kasper wanted to hear about my very first afternoon.
It was a cold afternoon in January.
I came up the stairs to my new apartment.
I had one very heavy suitcase.
I was very tired, and I was freezing.
I carried my suitcase up and inside myself.
A little later I stepped out into the stairwell.
A door next to mine opened.
A young woman came out and smiled at me.
"Hi, my name is Nina," she said.
"I also live here in the building."
I smiled back and said my name.
Nina lived right next to me.
We talked together a little in the stairwell.
It was nice to meet a neighbour right away.
"Welcome to Denmark," Nina said.
It was my first day here.
I was happy because I already had a friend.
